The problem is a variation of the partition problem, which is a classic dynamic programming task. If the sum of the list is odd, it is impossible to split it into two equal integer subsets. If the sum is even, the goal is to find a subset that sums to total_sum / 2. Using a boolean set or a bitmask can efficiently track reachable sums while iterating through the elements to optimize performance.

