[[ ## reasoning ## ]]
To satisfy the requirements, I will create a base class `Object`. I will define a `Motor` class to be used as a member variable (composition) within the `Vehicle` base class. `Vehicle` will inherit from `Object` and provide virtual functions to facilitate polymorphism. The subclasses `Car`, `Boat`, and `Airplane` will inherit from `Vehicle`, each adding specific attributes and overriding base methods. I will use encapsulation by making attributes private and providing getter/setter methods. Finally, the main function will use base class pointers to demonstrate polymorphic behavior through a list of vehicle objects.

