The first approach uses the "Schema-per-tenant" pattern in PostgreSQL, which provides strong logical isolation. This script creates a template schema, a specific role for the tenant to own that schema, and configures permissions so that the tenant can only interact with their own namespace, while a superuser or application role manages the schema creation.

